  40:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_fir_decimate_fast_q15.c **** /**
  41:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_fir_decimate_fast_q15.c ****  * @brief Processing function for the Q15 FIR decimator (fast variant) for Cortex-M3 and Cortex-M4.
  42:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_fir_decimate_fast_q15.c ****  * @param[in] *S points to an instance of the Q15 FIR decimator structure.
  43:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_fir_decimate_fast_q15.c ****  * @param[in] *pSrc points to the block of input data.
  44:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_fir_decimate_fast_q15.c ****  * @param[out] *pDst points to the block of output data
  45:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_fir_decimate_fast_q15.c ****  * @param[in] blockSize number of input samples to process per call.
  46:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_fir_decimate_fast_q15.c ****  * @return none
  47:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_fir_decimate_fast_q15.c ****  *
  48:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_fir_decimate_fast_q15.c ****  * \par Restrictions
  49:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_fir_decimate_fast_q15.c ****  *  If the silicon does not support unaligned memory access enable the macro UNALIGNED_SUPPORT_DISA
  50:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_fir_decimate_fast_q15.c ****  *	In this case input, output, state buffers should be aligned by 32-bit
  51:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_fir_decimate_fast_q15.c ****  *
  52:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_fir_decimate_fast_q15.c ****  * <b>Scaling and Overflow Behavior:</b>
  53:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_fir_decimate_fast_q15.c ****  * \par
  54:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_fir_decimate_fast_q15.c ****  * This fast version uses a 32-bit accumulator with 2.30 format.
  55:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_fir_decimate_fast_q15.c ****  * The accumulator maintains full precision of the intermediate multiplication results but provides
  56:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_fir_decimate_fast_q15.c ****  * Thus, if the accumulator result overflows it wraps around and distorts the result.
  57:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_fir_decimate_fast_q15.c ****  * In order to avoid overflows completely the input signal must be scaled down by log2(numTaps) bit
  58:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_fir_decimate_fast_q15.c ****  * The 2.30 accumulator is then truncated to 2.15 format and saturated to yield the 1.15 result.
  59:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_fir_decimate_fast_q15.c ****  *
  60:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_fir_decimate_fast_q15.c ****  * \par
  61:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_fir_decimate_fast_q15.c ****  * Refer to the function <code>arm_fir_decimate_q15()</code> for a slower implementation of this fu
  62:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_fir_decimate_fast_q15.c ****  * Both the slow and the fast versions use the same instance structure.
  63:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_fir_decimate_fast_q15.c ****  * Use the function <code>arm_fir_decimate_init_q15()</code> to initialize the filter structure.
  64:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_fir_decimate_fast_q15.c ****  */
  65:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_fir_decimate_fast_q15.c **** 
  66:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_fir_decimate_fast_q15.c **** #ifndef UNALIGNED_SUPPORT_DISABLE
